+**Your findings.** Each has a to-do test in test/beta-methodology-2.test.js or test/beta-methodology.test.js. Turn each to-do into a plain test that fails on the old code and passes after your fix, and mark the finding fixed in its review log with your commit.
+1. **MR-38 and MR-33 (High).** Fixed-term pay is converted to a yearly-looking figure.
+   - 182 internships post monthly or hourly pay with no stated length, and they are shown as yearly salaries; 111 of them get a yearly Juice score.
+   - An internship paid by the month with no stated length is fixed-term pay, not a yearly salary.
+   - The drawer's converted line for fixed-term pay must use the posted interval, or say "a year" plainly.
+   - If the normalizer changes, bump NORMALIZER_VERSION once and re-baseline the golden files with the tooling, never by hand. Say how many hashes changed and why.
+   - Show before and after counts per board, and prove nothing was dropped.
+2. **MR-37.** Austria's stated annual figure ("14 payments") has no "As posted" line. The drawer must explain a stated annual figure.
+3. **MR-39.** The headline medians mix countries. Say which country a headline median is for, or compute it per the board's home country, as the market cells do. This means the stats line, Insights' tiles and the chart caption. fix-viz-5 owns the chart's drawing, so coordinate through the lead if you change its caption.
+4. **MR-40.** Garden City NY, Fort Lee NJ and Paramus NJ geocode to their state's centre, so they miss Microsoft's NYC-metro pay area. Add them to the gazetteer in server/geo.js, and check for other NYC-metro towns that fall the same way.
+5. **MR-29, the UI half.** Google's departments are derived from job titles, and only the filter panel and a hover title say so. Say it once where the departments are read: the chart rows' notes or the stats line's Details. Keep the one-line rule; no new visible control.
+6. **MR-41.** The "Mid" chip's tip names "III" as mid level, but III is Senior at Amazon. Give an example that holds on every board, or a per-board example.
+7. **MR-26.** The methodology table shows Gross pay as "update due" on a freshly built site. Fix the freshness rule for build-day data.
+8. **MR-21 and MR-22.** registry.js's usage header must list every mode (--docs). market.json's fx.source must name the rate source, not a code path.
